+`gh api -X POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets --input .github/rulesets/static.json` creates the `static` ruleset: `main` then requires the `static` check from GitHub Actions, and the repository admin role is its one bypass, because every tracker push (`./zn status`, `land`, `done`, the dispatcher's broker) goes straight to `main`. `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/rules/branches/main` shows it. A pull request opened before `static.yml` reached `main` reports no `static` check until it runs again: push to its branch (a merge of `origin/main` does), or close and reopen it. When `main` itself fails the stages, every pull request's `static` fails until `main` is fixed, and then each needs a new run the same way (`gh run rerun` judges the old merge again). `gh api -X DELETE repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets/<id>` removes it.
 
