@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+title: A hand merge runs the static stages on the head first, because GitHub's checks are not the gate
+when: both
+tags: [merge, gate, format, lint, stylua, selene, github]
+check: Before this `gh pr merge` (or the merge button), did `z-nile/check.sh --lint` exit 0 on the pull request's head merged with `origin/main`, whatever GitHub's checks say?
+---
+GitHub's checks are not the gate. Until c0359 the only workflow, `deploy.yml`, ran none of it, so every pull request showed green whatever its files held. The required `static` check (c0359) now runs the format and lint stages, but it is a floor: it judged the merge as it stood at the last push, and the repository admin can bypass it. Whoever merges by hand runs the stages on the head first.
+
+**Why:** on 2026-11-15 Claude merged 28 prep pull requests by hand on green checks. Four of them (#397, #399, #408, #417) carried unformatted specs and selene warnings, so `main` failed `stylua --check` on 16 files and `selene` on two warnings until #433, and the user's `./zn done` was refused on files outside its raft. c0292's E3 had named three of those pull requests as failing before they merged. The user: "Learn a lesson from this and make sure it can't happen again".
+
+**How to apply:** in the pull request's worktree, or a clone of its exact head, merge `origin/main`, run `z-nile/check.sh --lint`, and fix what it names on the branch until it exits 0; check that `gh pr checks <pr> --required` passes (the merge state GitHub shows the admin may not say `BLOCKED`); read what other designs say about the pull request (a prep's Existing work may name it). Then merge, never with `--admin`. A pull request that changes the checker itself (`static.yml`, the gate's stages, the tools' settings) passes its own copy: run `main`'s `--lint` on it. While `main` fails the stages, every pull request's `static` fails; once `main` is fixed, each needs a push or a close and reopen (`gh run rerun` judges the old merge). The dispatcher's prep and raft gates run the same command on the merge (zz-rules skill, Dispatch).
